### the preprint against itself: the same quantity twice
==============================================================================
Quantities the preprint gives two values for
==============================================================================
  Both values in every row are the preprint's own, and so is the
  arithmetic between them.

  1. The absorption edge of the fission donor
       section 2.2        2.25 eV (551 nm), stated
       section 6.2        1.96 eV (634 nm), the edge its own 23.8 mA/cm^2
                          needs at its own EQE_high = 1.53
       disagreement       294 meV

  2. E(S1) of the donor
       section 2.2        2.25 eV, stated
       section 2.1        at least 2.30 eV, required by E(S1) >= 2 E(T1)
       disagreement       50 meV, so the fission is endothermic by 1.9 kT

  3. Electrons per absorbed photon above the edge
       section 6.2        1.53, stated as EQE_high = 153%
       section 6.2        2.44, required by its own 23.8 mA/cm^2 over the
                          9.76 mA/cm^2 the spectrum carries above 2.25 eV
       disagreement       59%, and 22% over fission's own ceiling of two

  4. tau_ext, the extraction transit time
       section 4.1        20 to 80 ns, stated
       section 4.1        256 ns, required by its own eta_PB = 0.95 through
                          its own eta_PB = exp(-tau_ext / tau_s), tau_s = 5 us
       disagreement       a factor 3.2 to 12.8, in the preprint's favour

  5. eta_PB, the same inconsistency read the other way
       section 4.1        0.95, stated
       section 4.1        0.9841 to 0.9960, from the two times in the same
                          sentence; the suppression is then 71.1%, not 68.6%
       disagreement       2.5 points of suppression, in the preprint's favour

  6. Carrier mobility of the active layer
