==============================================================================
What holds
==============================================================================
  The same test applied to every other quantity that appears twice.
  Each of these is a single expression evaluated inside one
  sentence, and each comes out right:

  quantity                                recomputed  as published     check
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------
  EQE_high = 1.85 x 0.92 x 0.90               1.5318  153% (6.2)       ok
  1 - eta_PB P_CISS^2                         0.3136  0.314 (4.1)      ok
  the suppression that follows                 68.6%  68.6% (4.1)      ok
  P_CISS of the worked example                  0.85  0.75-0.90 (3.2)  ok
  splitting of table 1                        0.8 eV  0.5-1.0 eV (5.1) ok
  V_oc = 0.90 V - 0.09 V                      0.81 V  0.81 V (6.2)     ok
  PCE = J_sc V_oc FF / P_in                   35.58%  35.58% (6.2)     ok
  2 E(T1) >= 2 E_g(IR), the second link 2.30 >= 2.24 eV  required by 2.2  ok

  8 of 8 hold.  Every arithmetic step the preprint performs it
  performs correctly.  What disagrees is never the algebra; it is
  always the numbers put into it.

==============================================================================
Row 1 is not an inconsistency but an exclusion
==============================================================================
  The other seven rows could each be repaired by choosing one of
  the two values.  Row 1 cannot, because section 2.2's own
  thermodynamic ordering fixes which value is allowed:

      E(S1_D) >= 2 E(T1_D) >= 2 E_CT >= 2 E_g(IR)

  2 E_g(IR) = 2.24 eV, so the chain forbids any donor whose S1 lies
  below that.  The edge its photocurrent needs is 1.96 eV, which is
  284 meV below the floor.

  Read the other way, a donor with E(S1) = 1.96 eV may have at most
  E(T1) = 0.98 eV, and that is 142 meV *below* the 1.12 eV gap of
  the acceptor it is supposed to feed, so the Dexter step of
  section 2.2 would run uphill and the cascade would not exist.

  So the two values are mutually exclusive rather than merely
  different: either the high-energy channel carries 14.95 mA/cm^2
  and not 23.8, or the energy cascade the architecture is built
  from is thermodynamically forbidden.  Nothing outside the
  preprint is needed to reach that.
